    <!-- Dialog messages -->
    <string name="remote_dialog_msg_password_vps_note">Just like a real VPS: while this is enabled, no one gets in with just the password — not even you, from another device without the matching key.</string>
    <string name="remote_dialog_msg_cambiar_puerto">sshd runs without root permissions — only ports 1024-65535 are allowed.</string>
    <string name="remote_dialog_msg_requerir_clave">The device will act as a real server (VPS): no one will be able to log in over SSH with just the password — not even you, from another device without the matching key. Make sure you already added your key under \"Add public key\".</string>
    <string name="remote_dialog_msg_permitir_login_root">This allows logging in over SSH directly as root, a real risk if the device is exposed to the internet (tunnel/VPS). Only enable it if you know what you\'re doing.</string>
    <string name="remote_dialog_msg_borrar_conexion">Delete \"%1$s\" (%2$s@%3$s:%4$d)? This does not affect the remote server, it just stops being saved here.</string>
    <string name="remote_dialog_msg_importar_clave_privada">It is saved on the device with restricted permissions (600). Once saved, Kairos never shows it again — you can only use it, replace it, or delete it.</string>
    <string name="remote_dialog_msg_borrar_clave_importada">Delete key \"%1$s\"? Saved connections that used it will ask for an interactive password next time.</string>
    <string name="remote_dialog_msg_conectar_clave_sesion">The key is NOT saved on the device — it\'s used only for this connection and deletes itself in a few seconds.</string>

